class.description:
A [LocalizationCatalog] is a table: one row per key (a key and an optional context) and one column per locale. [TextLocalizationCatalog] stores texts, [ResourceLocalizationCatalog] stores localized resource paths. Rows are addressed by key and context, or by their row number (see [method find_key]). The data is stored compactly: every locale is one column of UTF-8 text with one 4-byte offset per row, so a message costs its text plus 4 bytes (instead of an interned [StringName] per message like in [Translation]). [b]Files:[/b] [method load_from_file] and [method save_to_file] choose the format by the file extension. The binary [code].lcat[/code] format stores one block per locale: a catalog loaded from it (also with [method @GDScript.load]) reads only the keys and the locale table; the text of a locale is read when it is first used, or with [method load_locale]. This keeps unused locales out of memory and works from the PCK and [code]user://[/code] on every platform, including the Web. [b]Text formats[/b] ([method load_from_text], [method to_text], [enum ResourceTextSerializer.Format]): - CSV: the layout of Godot's CSV translation importer. Column 0 holds the keys, every other column a locale. A [code]?context[/code] column holds the context, a [code]?plural[/code] column the plural key (text catalogs) and starts plural rows, a [code]?type[/code] column holds the expected type (resource catalogs). Columns starting with [code]_[/code] are translator notes (the importer ignores them), a row starting with [code]?pluralrule[/code] holds the plural rule per locale. Translations are unescaped with [method String.c_unescape], keys are not. Without [SerializerOptions], the delimiter ([code],[/code], [code];[/code] or tab) is the one found most often in the header row. Empty cells and empty locale columns are missing translations, not errors. An empty catalog is written as [code]keys,?context,<locale>[/code] with the locale of [method TranslationServer.get_tool_locale] (in the editor, its language). - JSON, YAML, TOML, INI: one entry per key, [code]key: {locale: text}[/code]; plural forms are an array. Fields starting with [code]_[/code] are not locales: [code]_context[/code], [code]_key[/code] (the key, when the entry name differs from it, as for [code]"BACK@menu"[/code]), [code]_plural[/code] (text catalogs) or [code]_type[/code] (resource catalogs); other fields starting with [code]_[/code] are translator notes. The entry [code]?catalog[/code] holds [code skip-lint]locales[/code] (their order), [code]plural_rules[/code], [code skip-lint]channel[/code] and [code skip-lint]notes[/code] (the note columns, also those without notes yet). In INI, every key is a [code][section][/code]. - XML: [code]<catalog locales="en,de"><message key="HELLO" context="menu"><text locale="de">Hallo</text></message></catalog>[/code], one [code]<text>[/code] per plural form, [code]<plural_rule locale="de">[/code] elements for the plural rules, [code]<note name="notes">[/code] elements in a message for translator notes. [b]Translator notes:[/b] columns or fields such as [code]_notes[/code] or [code]_max_length[/code] hold notes per key for translators and tools (see [method get_note]). They are kept by every text format and in [code].tres[/code], but never written to [code].lcat[/code], and a catalog loaded through [ResourceLoader] outside the editor (as the localization servers do) skips them, so they cost no memory in a game. [method load_from_file] and [method load_from_text] always keep them. Saved as [code].tres[/code] or [code].res[/code], a catalog stores all locales in one block (no loading per locale). [codeblocks] [gdscript] var catalog = TextLocalizationCatalog.new() catalog.load_from_file("res://translations/ui.csv") catalog.save_to_file("user://ui.lcat")
var lazy = load("user://ui.lcat") as TextLocalizationCatalog print(lazy.is_locale_loaded("de")) # false print(lazy.get_text("HELLO", "de")) # Loads "de" only. [/gdscript] [csharp] var catalog = new TextLocalizationCatalog(); catalog.LoadFromFile("res://translations/ui.csv"); catalog.SaveToFile("user://ui.lcat");
var lazy = GD.Load<TextLocalizationCatalog>("user://ui.lcat"); GD.Print(lazy.IsLocaleLoaded("de")); // false GD.Print(lazy.GetText("HELLO", "de")); // Loads "de" only. [/csharp] [/codeblocks] [b]Editor:[/b] a catalog opened in the inspector is edited in the Localization Table dock (one row per key, one column per locale and note column, plural forms as child rows, undo/redo); the inspector lists the missing keys per locale. In the FileSystem dock, "Use as Text Localization Catalog" / "Use as Resource Localization Catalog" adds data files to [member ProjectSettings.internationalization/localization/catalog_manifests] and opens them; Project > Tools > "Convert Project Translations to Catalogs..." moves the translations and translation remaps of the Localization tab to catalogs. On export, text catalogs of the manifests are converted to [code].lcat[/code] (see [member ProjectSettings.internationalization/localization/export/convert_text_to_binary]). [b]Note:[/b] [code].csv[/code] files in a project are imported by the CSV translation importer. To read them at runtime with [method load_from_file], set their import mode to "Keep File (exported as is)", or convert them to [code].lcat[/code]. [b]Note:[/b] Reading the same catalog from several threads is safe (loading a locale is guarded by a lock); changing it while other threads read it is not.

method.description:
Checks the catalog and returns the issues:
- [constant DataValidation.ISSUE_KIND_EMPTY_REQUIRED]: a key without text in a locale. Row = the key's row, column = the locale's index in [member locales], field = the locale.
- [constant DataValidation.ISSUE_KIND_DUPLICATE_KEY]: a key defined more than once in the text it was last loaded from (CSV rows, or entries whose [code]_key[/code] and [code]_context[/code] repeat another entry). The definitions were merged.
- [constant DataValidation.ISSUE_KIND_INVALID_LOCALE]: a locale column that is not a standard locale code of a known language. Column = its index, field = the locale.
The path of an issue is the entry name ([code]key[/code] or [code]key@context[/code]). For a catalog loaded from a text file through [ResourceLoader] (its [member Resource.resource_path] has a text extension), the issues get the line of their key in that file. [param options] limits the number of issues ([member DataValidationOptions.max_issues], [member DataValidationOptions.stop_on_first]); [method get_translated_count] counts the missing texts without a limit.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var result = catalog.validate()
for i in result.get_issue_count():
	print("%d: %s" % [result.get_issue_line(i), result.get_issue_message(i)])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
DataValidation result = catalog.Validate();
for (int i = 0; i < result.GetIssueCount(); i++)
{
	GD.Print($"{result.GetIssueLine(i)}: {result.GetIssueMessage(i)}");
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
